[GER.FullName]
Operation Citadel 
[GER.Description]
[GER.Epilogue]
July 9 was the last day when the Germans made any progress on the southern face of the Kursk salient towards Kursk. The turn made by the 2nd Tank Corps of the Waffen-SS through Prokhorovka led to a battle with the 5th Tank Army on July 12 and was unsuccessful. From the 10th to the 17th of July Grossdeutschland Division conducted fruitless battles on the line of Novenkoe, Kalinovka, and Novoselovka against the forces of the 6th Guards and 1st Guards Tank Armies. 
Captain Hartmann lost his best comrades-in-arms during those days: company commander Oberleutnant Autenrit, battalion adjutant Lieutenant Feldhaus, dozens of veteran non-commissioned officers and soldiers. It was especially bitter to part with the honorable commander Colonel Graf von Strachwitz, badly wounded in the attack on another unnamed hill. 

On July 18 Grossdeutschland Division was called back from the front and brought to the rear for rest and reinforcement. Later the division played the role of a "fire crew", deployed to the worst corners of the Eastern Front, from its Southern wing in Romania to the Northern wing near the Baltic. In 1944 Werner Hartmann was promoted to Major and appointed to division headquarters. In the winter of 1945 the division struggles for East Prussia. In March, Russian troops pressed the division against the sea in the vicinity of Heiligenbeil, Balga. Only 4,000 men were evacuated to Pillau from there. Here, in April 1945, the operational record of the Grossdeutschland Division ends. Only 800 men could escape to Schleswig-Holstein by ferry. Major Werner Hartmann was not among them. 

In the 1970s a bulldozer revealed a destroyed pillbox on the shore of the Curonian Lagoon at Mamonovo (former Heiligenbeil) in Kaliningrad region. Hartmann's remains and a diary hidden in a map case were found. The last entry in the diary was an address of the Grossdeutschland Division commander Major General Lorenz to his men, dated April 1945: 

The combat situation is completely under our control, in spite of the hard struggle and great difficulties. This battle has brightly highlighted your dedication, tactical efficiency, high spirit and camaraderie. I thank you for your honorable service in the days of the greatest peril for Germany. You have done the impossible for the glory of our unit, believing faithfully in the future of the German people...

[Ger_Cherkasskoe_south.Description]
\t Captain Werner Hartmann started as a full private in the tank forces of the Wehrmacht in 1936, from where he rose in the ranks. His first active service took place in Poland and Yugoslavia. From 1941 Werner fought on the Eastern Front in the Grossdeutschland Division where he earned the reputation of a decisive and experienced commander. Werner was a firm authority for his subordinates, a military lawyer for both the soldier and the officer. He commanded on the field with skill, tried to save both men and equipment, did everything possible to facilitate the grim military way of life of the tankman. He went through many trials on the battlefields of France, Yugoslavia, and Russia with many officers, tank commanders and regular tankmen and he trusted them as much as he trusted himself. 
\t July 5, 03:15. A long hush of expectancy for the beginning of the great battle to turn the tides of the war in favor of Germany had finally finished yesterday. During the last several months we had been preparing thoroughly for the forthcoming battles, but we could not shake the feeling that the long delay of the offensive was only to the advantage of the Russians. It seems that the Russians turned the Kursk salient into a real fortress. But the arrival of new modernized tanks and a company of Tigers under the command of Captain Wahlrot instills confidence in our success.
\t Grossdeutschland Division's battle yesterday for the frontline and vantage points revealed the increased power of the enemy. The enemy is dumbstruck, but defends well. Division commander General Hoernlein informed us, that we are to receive a brigade with 200 of the newest Panther tanks! We have discussed the news with the regiment's commander Graf von Strachwitz and decided that it would be better to give those vehicles to our experienced tankmen. Besides, the storm we had yesterday turned the lowland into impassable marshes, antitank ditches were filled with water, and that drastically hinders the movement of the vehicles. 
\t Colonel von Strachwitz expressed confidence that our battalion would fulfill the assigned tasks immaculately and would make a passage for the other units of the division. I assured the Graf that we would not spare ourselves in the battle for the Vaterland and would uphold the honor of the elite Wehrmacht unit. We will fight with our motto: "God, Honor, and the Fatherland". Half an hour ago I made a circuit of the camp, had a talk with the soldiers and officers. All are in a cheerful mood and absolutely ready to fulfill the Führer's order. The Kursk salient is to become a mass grave for the Russian armies.
\n 
\t SITUATION AND ORDER
\t On July 5 the 48th Tank Corps delivers the main blow in the direction of Butovo - Cherkasskoe in order to break through 6th Army defenses and reach the objective of Mikhaylovka - Yarki. 
\t Grossdeutschland Motorized Division with the support of the 39th tank regiment (Panther tanks) disrupts the defenses of 67th Guards Rifle Division, surrounds and destroys the enemy in Cherkasskoe. 
\t The tank regiment with a battalion from the rifle regiment attacks in the middle of the division's battle formations with the task of occupying the southern outskirts of Cherkasskoe.
\n 
\t COMBAT ORDER:
\t Up to a rifle battalion with antitank artillery and tanks holds the defensive positions in Cherkasskoe. The front line of the enemy defense lies 0.5km to the south of Cherkasskoe. Before the enemy front line there is an antitank ditch, a mine field and barbed wire. Counterattacks of the enemy response forces with up to a tank company are possible from the northwest. 
\t A combat team of tank and rifle companies, with Panther tank, assault and AA gun suport is being formed under the command of Captain Hartmann. 
\t Hartmann's combat team will take the southern outskirts of Cherkasskoe in a joint tank and infantry assault and take the village.
\n 
\t Concept of the operation: 
\t - pass the antitank ditch and minefields through the passage lanes; 
\t - flank enemy positions, destroy enemy defenses; 
\t - destroy enemy guns and infantry on the frontline; 
\t - reach the southern outskirts of Cherkasskoe and consolidate on the objective; 
\t - be ready to meet the counterattacks of enemy infantry from the flanks, tanks and assault guns from the front.
\n 
\t The offensive is supported with artillery fire and ground attack aircraft. Supporting fire will be according to coordination signals.
[Ger_Cherkasskoe_south.FullName]
Cherkasskoe, southern outskirts
[Ger_Cherkasskoe_north.Description]
\t July 5, 17:30. It seems like this bloody day will never end... The combat team of the regiment has been breaking through to the southern outskirts of Cherkasskoe since early morning. We managed to wrest ground from the enemy beyond the antitank ditches, but before the village the battalions were delayed by minefields and obstacles. The Russians are masters of disguise. Not a single mine, not a single tank-killing area was spotted until the first tank tripped a mine or the first Russian antitank gun opened fire. 
\t Just as Colonel von Strachwitz warned, Dekker's brigade of Panthers proved helpless. The commanders' lack of foresight led to the situation, where companies knew absolutely nothing about the attack plan. Panthers moved right into minefields, being shot by Russian antitank weapons. Ordering to charge to compensate for lost time, Dekker drove his brigade into an impassable bog. Our engineers are now trying to get them out of there.
\t When possibilities are gone forever, you can only grind your teeth. It would be nice to believe that God or fate will present those possibilities once more. I'm writing like this because in this battle, more than in any other battle, my thoughts are spinning round the ultimate importance of what is going on. Here, in one of the greatest battles in human history, the true Prussian spirit should be revealed in its final form. Herein, the best of Germany, gathered in the Wehrmacht, stand in the face of destiny and do not close their eyes at the sight. That destiny is perceived as a fatal call. We are in a bloodcurdling trial. The fate of the Russians was decided at Stalingrad. The fate of the German people is being decided here and now.
\n 
\t SITUATION AND ORDER
\t Grossdeutschland Motorized Division took the frontline positions of the 67th Guards Rifle Division to the south of Cherkasskoe. On the left flank, some troops with the support of the 39th Tank Regiment passed Cherkasskoe to the west and buckled an the junction point of the 67th and 71st Guards Rifle Divisions. On the right flank, in a joint attack with the 11th Tank Division, the forces managed to break through to the vicinity of Hill 246.0 eastward of Cherkasskoe. At 18:00 the division delivers the main blow in the direction Butovo - Cherkasskoe with the task of occupying Cherkasskoe by the end of the day with further advancement towards Yarki.
\n 
\t OPERATION ORDER:
\t Up to a rifle company with antitank artillery, antitank rifles and dug-in tanks defends Cherkasskoe. The front line of the enemy defense lies on the southern outskirts of Cherkasskoe. Supposedly, there are minefields before the enemy front line. An antitank strong point is in the forest, 0.5km to the northeast of Cherkasskoe. Tank reserves can approach from the direction of Alekseevka - Cherkasskoe. 
\t Captain Hartmann's combat team, reinforced with tanks and assault guns, occupies the original sector 1km to the south of Cherkasskoe. 
\t The combat team will occupy Cherkasskoe in a joint tank and infantry attack and proceed further towards Yarki.
\n 
\t Concept of operation: 
\t - suppress the firing positions on the frontline with ground attack aircraft and concentrated artillery fire; 
\t - overtake the enemy positions using flanking maneuvers; 
\t - destroy enemy weapons and infantry in the first trench; 
\t - after taking the first trench, redeploy units in battle formations and strike at the center of the village; 
\t - destroy the strong point and mortars in the forest 0.5km to the northeast of Cherkasskoe; 
\t - after taking the first positions, be ready to repel an enemy tank and SP gun flanking counterattack.
[Ger_Cherkasskoe_north.FullName]
Cherkasskoe 
[Ger_Syrcevo_Dubrovo_south.Description]
\t July 6, 13:00. Yesterday's and today's events have shown that the element of surprise, which was so much relied on in this battle, was lost. The Russians prepared solid defenses in the sectors we planned to rush through. As a result, our advance degenerates into the slow grinding of countless of antitank points. Yet since yesterday we have advanced 10 kilometers and captured, at last, the first defensive line, having reached the approaches to Dubrovo and Syrtsev in the afternoon. Sometimes I think that we have paid too dear a price for this. In the battle for Cherkasskoe my close comrade-in-arms, Major Graf Karl Anton Saurma was killed by an enemy shell. 
\t The enemy actions have changed drastically in the last months. As recently as in spring, under Kharkov, only separate groups of the Russians fought fanatically, others fled or quickly surrendered. It has all changed now: the Russians fight with horrifying resolution, whole units perish, but there are no signs of confusion or panic in their ranks. A Russian soldier fights until his last breath. Crews of smoking tanks keep firing until their last heartbeats. The wounded and shell-shocked grab weapons as soon as they regain their senses.
\t Yesterday the damned Panthers became a burden for von Strachwitz and the whole division - and they should be our ultimate strike force! The colonel was enraged; he defiantly ignored Dekker's attempts to reach him. This clash has had a bad influence on our operations. General Hoernlein was forced to approach the corps commander with an urgent request to place all Panthers under the command of von Strachwitz. General von Knobelsdorf conceded to these demands and suspended Dekker from command. Major von Lauhert's 39th regiment of Panthers is now under our full command. I have no doubts that von Strachwitz will find the best use for them, in keeping with the best traditions of German tank forces. 
\t Our task at hand is the second defense line of the Russians. According to reconnaissance, it is fortified as good as the one in the Cherkasskoe area. It is most likely the last obstacle in the direction of Oboyan and Kursk. We have to breach that wall before the Russians move up their reserves. Officers and soldiers are tired, but they do not lose confidence, they are sure that the key to victory is in our hands.
\n 
\t SITUATION AND ORDER
\t Grossdeutschland Motorized Division reached the antitank ditch 2km to the southwest of Dubrovo by 13:00 July 6. The main body should bear down on the Russian resistance along the road to Dubrovo and reach the eastern outskirts of Dubrovo. Then, by delivering a strike to the north in the direction of Syrtsev, it will cut off the enemy on the southern shore of the Pena river. Simultaneously, the second combat team will attack Lukhanino with the aim of breaking any resistance and surrounding the enemy forces in the sector of Kalashnoe, Lukhanino, and Syrtsev. 
\n 
\t OPERATION ORDER:
\t There is an antitank strong point with artillery, antitank guns and tanks on Hill 241.1 in front of Dubrovo. The front line of the enemy defense lies 100m to the north of the antitank ditch. There is a minefield in front of the ditch and the first trench. 
\t Captain Hartmann's combat team supported with tanks and assault guns will advance towards Hill 241.1, Dubrovo. Defeat the enemy at the strong point, then reach the eastern outskirts of Dubrovo.
\n 
\t Concept of operation: 
\t - division artillery neutralizes enemy forces positioned behind the antitank ditch; 
\t - in a decisive charge, with the support of artillery and engineers, pass the antitank ditch through passage lanes and flank the enemy positions; 
\t - suppress artillery and machine guns on the flanks with the concentrated fire of tanks and infantry; 
\t - a grenadier assault team will capture the hill summit and ensure the transit of the main force; 
\t - ensure that von Strachwitz's combat team is deployed in the direction of Dubrovo, Syrtsev; 
\t - prevent the enemy reserves from reaching the isolated positions; 
\t - be ready to repel enemy flanking counterattacks. 
\n 
\t The offensive is supported with ground attack aircraft and artillery fire. Supporting fire will be according to coordination signals.
[Ger_Syrcevo_Dubrovo_south.FullName]
Syrtsev-Dubrova line
[Ger_Syrcevo_Dubrovo_north_recon.Description]
\t Excerpts from the diary of Unteroffizier Rolf Steiner, Knight of the Iron Cross: 
\n 
\t Captain Hartmann ordered me to select a group of the most experienced guys and infiltrate the Russian positions to destroy their AA guns. Well, we are used to all kinds of "overwhelmingly important", "special" and "delicate" orders. I'm sure that if I call for volunteers, everyone will answer the summon, though all are dog-tired. 
\t Lengthy violent fighting turns a soldier into a dumb donkey, pulling stubbornly his burden. Human reasoning on the frontline is hypnotized by the war in some way. 
\t The feelings of danger and mercy subside or freeze entirely. A man underreacts to all monstrosities happening around him. I can't help grinning when I remember my foolish liveliness at the beginning of the campaign. Now I have another vision of things, the cynical view of an old war dog.
\t I learned how to determine the true situations in the lines of verbal diarrhea from "orientation officers". I remember how passionately they lied after the disaster at Stalingrad. Today one of those "nightingales of Goebbels" claimed: "Schutz-Staffel men have already penetrated to the vicinity of Kursk, and the victory is almost in the hands of the Wehrmacht". I understood instantly, that things went wrong, and the offensive failed. It looks like the operation was destined to fail since the very beginning. Looking at hundreds of tanks, raising dust from the roads, and hordes of German infantry, dragging themselves through endless Russian fields under the blazing sun, I'm reminded of the poem by Heinrich Heine:
\n 
\t \t There are two kinds of rat:
\t \t One hungry and one fat.
\t \t The fat one stays content at home,
\t \t But hungry ones go out and roam.
\t \t These wild and savage rats
\t \t Fear neither hell nor cats;
\t \t They have no property or money too,
\t \t So they want to divide the world anew.
\t \t These roving rats, alas!
\t \t Are near us now en masse
\t \t I hear their squeaks - straight on they press -
\t \t Their multitude is numberless.
\n 
\t It looks like it is time for the rats to think about saving their asses in this slaughter. What the hell are we doing here? All we can do is to keep soldiering on, trying to save our own lives and the lives of our comrades-in-arms. Our company is like a united family. There's no privacy here, everyone knows each other well, everyone can trust each other, and everyone hopes, that his Kamerad will help him in the minute of danger. I find myself thinking that I know the feelings and thoughts of the soldiers of my platoon better, than I know thoughts and feelings of my parents and my wife...
\n 
\t SITUATION AND ORDER
\t The enemy has moved up the 9th AA Artillery Division from the rear to the sector of Syrtsev, Verkhopenye, Sukho-Solotino, Novoselovka. The enemy division is equipped with a large number of 3.7cm and 8.5cm AA guns. Deploying a potent air defense system in the path of the Grossdeutschland Division's main advance endangers the possibility of enjoying ground attack aircraft support in tomorrow's offensive. 
\t Division commander General Hoernlein has ordered that a sabotage reconnaissance group be dispatched from each regiment at night with the task of destroying air defense command posts and taking out as many AA guns as possible.
\n 
\t OPERATION ORDER:
\t - Unteroffizier Steiner will personally select and head a group of high-skilled soldiers for a sabotage-reconnaissance mission; 
\t - under cover of deceptive small arms and mortar fire on the adjacent sector infiltrate through the enemy frontline to the sector of the enemy AA battery in the vicinity of Dubrovo; 
\t - in a sudden strike kill the AA gun crews, thus ensuring safe passage for our ground attack aircraft; 
\t - communication is according to the adopted signals and frequencies list; 
\t - the sabotage-reconnaissance group is supported by a mortar battery and ground attack aircraft; 
\t - the password for returning through our frontline is "Demarcation".
[Ger_Syrcevo_Dubrovo_north_recon.FullName]
A place where Iron Crosses grow
[Ger_Syrcevo_Dubrovo_north.Description]
\t July 7, 06:00 Now it is absolutely evident, that the Syrtsev - Dubrovo line is the main Soviet line of defense with most of their units dug-in along its length. We have to fight through antitank ditches, minefields, trenches, hidden artillery positions. At dawn today von Strachwitz's brigade came under heavy fire from artillery and Stalin's organs in the vicinity of Dubrovo, which forced us to postpone the offensive to 09:00 and request Stukas action to suppress the enemy. 
\t Three days of heavy fighting without a minute of rest has exhausted the forward troops. You cannot relax once you've reached the objective, as the Russians counterattack at once with large groups of tanks, trying to flank us. Owing to our magnificent reconnaissance we block the directions of counterattacks in time and repel those ruthless charges. Air reconnaissance reports that the Soviets are moving large forces to the Oboyan sector. We should break through their defenses as soon as possible, before the enemy takes up new positions. Our task at hand is to clear the defending units, which will give us maneuvering space. We should break out of the trap of exhausting fights for every hill and every village. 
\t Placing the Panthers under von Strachwitz's command did good for us. The task force commanders of the brigade are not yet experienced enough and they often commit blunders, but operational command, at least, prevents senseless maneuvers and doesn't waste time. Yesterday we finally received real combat aid from the Panthers and obtained good results. 
\t Extreme fatigue and insomnia give sometimes rise to abstract thoughts about the understanding of all these events. The war became a natural phenomenon, just like the rain or the wind. And we are just a miniscule part of the phenomenon. We appeared somewhere in its bowels, and when it wanes, our existence could be finished as well. Though it was we who began the war, eventually it infiltrated our souls and made us its puppets. It burned away a lot in us, and it keeps subtracting something important out of each of us until we degenerate into something new. You cannot fight it; you should not look back, it would only make your heart ache. All we can do is open our souls to its force and fulfill its orders. 
\n 
\t SITUATION AND ORDER
\t July 7, 07:00 Grossdeutschland Motorized Division is standing before an antitank ditch to the southwest of Hill 254.5. To the right, 11th Tank Division is moving along the road to Oboyan in two combat teams. It has reached the south slopes of the hills to the east of Dubrovo. To the left, 3rd Tank Division is preparing for a combat crossing of the Pena and establishing positions in the vicinity of Lukhanino. 
\t The main body of division will take Hill 254.5 in an assault from the southwest and advance north. Simultaneously, the second combat team will destroy the enemy forces on the southern shore of the Pena by attacking in the northwest in the direction of Syrtsev. It will then advance toward 3rd Tank Division to surround the enemy in the sector to the northeast of Lukhanino. 
\n 
\t COMBAT ORDER:
\t The enemy holds his positions to the northwest of Dubrovo and in the vicinity of Syrtsev with infantry and antitank artillery. Tanks were not spotted. The front line lies on the eastern border of Syrtsev. Minefields are possible on the flanks of the strong point. The movement of up to 100 enemy tanks on the road Ivnya, Verkhopenye has been spotted. 
\t Captain Hartmann's combat team with tank and assault gun support will advance towards Dubrovo - Syrtsev, bypassing Syrtsev to the north. Defeat the enemy at Syrtsev, then reach the eastern shore of the Pena to the north of Syrtsev. Destroy the command post of the Soviet brigade in Syrtsev at all costs.
\n 
\t Concept of operation: 
\t - division artillery suppresses the enemy on the frontline with concentrated fire; 
\t - under the cover of artillery fire the combat team passes Syrtsev to the east and strikes at the junction of the defensive positions; 
\t - then it flanks the strong point in Syrtsev; 
\t - in a simultaneous attack from the flank and from the front overtake the enemy positions in Syrtsev; 
\t - proceed further to the eastern shore of the Pena and inhibit enemy attacks from the north; 
\t - artillery and tank fire suppresses the enemy on the western shore of the Pena; 
\t - prepare to advance towards 3rd Tank Division, offensive begins only after 3rd Tank Division has established a foothold in Lukhanino. 
\n 
\t The offensive is supported with ground attack air force and artillery fire. Supporting fire will be according to coordination signals.
[Ger_Syrcevo_Dubrovo_north.FullName]
Assault on Syrtsev 
[Ger_Syrcevo_Dubrovo_north_1.Description]
\t July 7, 06:00 Now it is absolutely evident, that the Syrtsev - Dubrovo line is the main Soviet line of defense with most of their units dug-in along its length. We have to fight through antitank ditches, minefields, trenches, hidden artillery positions. At dawn today von Strachwitz's brigade came under heavy fire from artillery and Stalin's organs in the vicinity of Dubrovo, which forced us to postpone the offensive to 09:00 and request Stukas action to suppress the enemy. 
