[Ger_Syrcevo_Dubrovo_north_1.FullName]
Assault on Syrtsev 
[Ger_Verhopenye_south.Description]
\t July 8, dawn. Today I have received a letter from my dearest wife Gretchen:
\n 
\t My dear Werner, yesterday I was happy to receive another letter from you. I write in hope 
that you are still safe and sound. So, my dear Werner, aren't you going to finish off 
the Russians once and for all? We count on it all the time. Maybe you'll come home on vacation then? Weekly newsreels show us how awful they are, one can hardly look at them. It is a shame that such disgusting rabble populate the Earth; you get sick when you see the dreadful faces 
of the captives. Well, enough about that. I have an awful headache, and it's no surprise with the 
weather like this. I can see how hot it must be where you are. 
\t \t \t \t \t \t \t \t \t \t \t \t \t \t Yours, Gretchen.
\n 
\t Our tank regiment suffers heavy losses from Russian antitank fire and countless mines. By last night, only 31 tanks remained in service. Battalion commander Captain Wilhelm von Gottberg is seriously wounded, and he had replaced the former commander, Graf Saurma, who died in his tank heroically, only a day ago. The grenadier regiment lost the battalion adjutant Lieutenant Holzgreve; one or two officers remained in the infantry companies. One of the battalions of the rifle regiment has its third commander in only several days of the offensive! 
\t It's bitter to know that we are losing the salt of the earth. Yesterday a shell fragment cut short the life of Feldwebel Otto Greiner, knight of the Iron Cross. I saw a lot of action shoulder to shoulder with that brave German soldier in France, Yugoslavia, and the Eastern Front. That's why I deem it my duty to personally inform his father about the tragedy:
\n 
\t \t My dear Herr Greiner!
\t In a severe fight with the enemy, your son, Feldwebel Otto Greiner, true to the oath and his 
soldier's duty, died heroically for the Führer and the Vaterland on July 7, 1943 in the vicinity of 
Syrtsev. 
\t Our comrade-in-arms Otto Greiner was one of the veterans of the battalion, which only 
makes our bereavement greater. I know, my dear Herr Greiner, about the sorrow the death 
of this soldier brings to your family. With my heart open, I offer you my deepest sympathy on 
behalf of the whole battalion. We will never forget your dearest Otto Greiner. We have the 
unrelenting conviction that the death of Feldwebel Greiner was not in vain. He sacrificed his 
life for the sake of our motherland's freedom, our fatherlands' security, and the Great German 
Reich's future.
\n 
\t SITUATION AND ORDER
\t The valley ahead of the Grossdeutschland Division to the southeast of Syrtsev is occupied with tanks, antitank guns and Stalin's organs. The division advances to the north and northeast and occupies the line from Hill 230.1 to the northeastern part of Syrtsev. The Panzerfuesiliere regiment occupies a clearing to the north of Olkhovaya valley northwest of the Syrtsev. The grenadier regiment with its reconnaissance detachment is to the north and to the west of Gremuchy. There is a tank brigade between the two regiments, which has engaged a strong enemy tank group to the southeast of Syrtsev.
\n 
\t COMBAT ORDER:
\t To the southeast of Verkhopenye, on the hills to the east of the Pena the enemy holds improvised defensive positions with infantry, antitank artillery and tanks. Large tank forces have been spotted on the western shore of the Pena in the sectors to the north and to the west of Verkhopenye. 
\t The main body of the 48th Tank Corps breaks through the enemy defenses to the east of Syrtsevo and prevents the enemy withdrawal in the direction of Oboyan with a northward attack. Grossdeutschland continues the assault on Syrtsevo and after it has been occupied breaks further through to the north and northeast in the direction of Verkhopenye and the road to the west of Pokrovka. 

\t Captain Hartmann's combat team with the support of von Strachwitz's tank brigade will advance towards Syrtsevo, Verkhopenye along the eastern shore of the Pena to the north of Syrtsevo.
\n 
\t Concept of operation: 
\t - the main body is supported by the 70th artillery regiment, 109th mortar and 842nd gun battalion; 
\t - under the cover of artillery fire the combat team will advance to the northern slopes of the Syrtsevo - Gremyachy valley and attack the enemy positions to the south and to the east of Verkhopenye; 
\t - after this it will secure the left flank of the division from enemy counterattacks directed from the western shore of the Pena; 
\t - moving northward, clear the enemy from the eastern shore of the Pena; 
\t - having reached Verkhopenye, consolidate on the objective, preventing attacks from the north; 
\t - on the right flank, protect the junction with von Strachwitz's brigade, which advances in the center; 
\t - if necessary, strike at the rear of the enemy tank group in front of von Strachwitz's brigade from the Verkhopenye sector. 
\n 
\t The offensive is supported with ground attack aircraft and artillery fire. Supporting fire will be according to coordination signals.
[Ger_Verhopenye_south.FullName]
To the south of Verkhopenye
[Ger_Verhopenye_north.Description]
\t July 8, 14:00. In the afternoon we finally broke through the Soviet defenses to the west of the road to Oboyan and captured the main hill. The enemy retreats to Novoselovka and to the western shore of the Pena river. These battles, with heavy casualties, are very similar to the battles of the Great War. Logistic support and mass assaults are the Russians' favorite tactics, they regard them as crucial advantages. But their attempts crash against the iron will and tireless strength of our forces. The deeds of valor our superior infantry accomplishes every day are indescribable. It's an ode to bravery, courage and moderation. 
\t In the battles we have fully realized that the only way to achieve any results in breaking through the defensive lines of the Russians is to concentrate tank forces on a restricted front with intensive and unceasing air support. At the same time, armored vehicles remain the most reliable mean for repelling Soviet counterattacks. In many cases, tank regiments turn into fire crews, saving the day in hot spots. 
\t Unfortunately, our forces are not infinite. Our strike force, von Strachwitz's brigade, lost too many tanks. They told us at division headquarters, that they cannot spare enough vehicles to support us, as only 31 battle-worthy tanks are left in the tank regiments, including only one Tiger. The regiment of Panthers is literally in a disastrous state, having only about 40 tanks intact.
\t General Hoernlein allotted us the very demanding task of establishing a bridgehead on the western shore by Verkhopenye, with the goal of creating the conditions to surround the Russian tank corps together with the 3rd Tank Division, advancing from the area of Lukhanino, Syrtsev. As soon as possible we must secure the left flank of the corps threatened by Russian tanks and under fire from Soviet artillery on the western shore. Stalin's organs have become so bold lately, that they fire in direct view of our tanks from the hills in the vicinity of Verkhopenye. 
\t Reconnaissance reports that there are 25 enemy tanks moving to the sector. According to intercepted messages, the enemy orders are to hold the western shore of the Pena by any means and deny our crossing. Our task is difficult, but the German soldier has always dealt with any obstacle.
\n 
\t SITUATION AND ORDER
\t Grossdeutschland Division is conducting violent tank fighting in the sector to the west of Verkhopenye. The main body of 11th Tank Division is in the vicinity of Stanovaya landmark. The grenadier regiment of the Grossdeutschland Division has occupied the southern part of Verkhopenye. The northern part of Syrtsev on the left flank is occupied by the Panzerfuesiliere regiment. 
\t The enemy is moving his tank reserves to the northern part of Verkhopenye, groups of infantry drop back to the village from the eastern shore of the Pena. Artillery in force is in the hills westward from Verkhopenye. An antitank line is deployed on the western shore of the Pena.
\n 
\t COMBAT ORDER:
\t Tanks and artillery with poor infantry support hold the line on the western shore of the Pena in the area of Verkhopenye and to the north of it. Separate battle outposts are spotted on the eastern shore of the Pena. 
\t The main body of 48th Tank Corps advances northward on each side of the roadway to Oboyan. Grossdeutschland continues the offensive along the western side of the roadway in the direction of Novoselovka. Having reached the line of Ilyinsky, Verkhopenye its left flank turns to Verkhopenye and establishes a bridgehead on the western shore of the Pena. 
\t Hartmann's combat team with its assigned tanks will advance along the eastern shore of the Pena, clearing out the sector to the east of Verkhopenye with the aim to secure the left flank of the division. After that, it will attack the western part of Verkhopenye and win a crossing across the Pena. Immediately report about establishing a bridgehead to corps headquarters in order to organize mutual support with 3rd Tank Division, advancing from Lukhanino.
\n 
\t Combat concept: 
\t - reinforcements: a company of Panthers, a battery of assault guns, 109th mortar battalion; 
\t - covered by artillery and assault weapons from the left flank, the combat team advances northward along the shore of the Pena and destroys enemy positions in the sector to the east of Verkhopenye; 
\t - then it secures the left flank of the division from enemy counterattacks from the north; 
\t - the combat team attacks and wins crossings across the Pena; 
\t - having established a bridgehead on the western shore, the team holds it until the division's main forces arrive; 
\t - if it proves impossible to take the western shore, the team is to secure a foothold on the eastern shore and denies the enemy access to the bridge.
[Ger_Verhopenye_north.FullName]
Verkhopenye
[Ger_Novoselovka.Description]
\t July 9, dawn. Today is the day. According to the original Operation Citadel plan, it is today that we were to encircle the Russian armies, and meet Model's army in the vicinity of Kursk. But the strategic objectives had been forgotten as soon as the operation began. The scope of our intentions and plans had been narrowed day by day. As of today we have to concentrate on local tactical objectives such as occupying small villages and hills. The neverending Soviet tank counterattacks compel us to pay careful attention to flank security, which requires large infantry and antitank artillery forces. The front of our offensive narrows, the prospect of breaking out with our mobile teams fades. 
\t Yesterday's battle for Verkhopenye proved that the Soviets managed to move artillery and tanks up to the last defensive line. They gave our brave troops not a single chance to break through to the western shore of the Pena. The enemy doesn't only defend; he attacks us with large tank units from the northeast, north and northwest and on the right flank as well. It seems like his intention is to hit from the flank and to cut off the combat teams, advanced to the north. Today we have to consider the continuation of ruthless tank attacks from the same directions. Under such conditions, the advance of 5-6km northward we made yesterday looks like a significant gain.
\t Often Soviet counterattack tactics are too straightforward: insane charges of infantry and tanks, poorly organized, at every opportunity, against known superior forces of our tanks and artillery. But on the organized defense lines the Russians stand firm, and penetrating them results into too many losses. Unfortunately, the best soldiers and officers of the Wehrmacht, veterans of many victorious campaigns died in those violent fights. It is evident that there are big problems with fulfilling operation Citadel's objectives. The offensive stalls, casualties increase, and we can only dream about reinforcements. I'm not too pious, but today I'm going to pray for luck. Gott mit uns!
\n 
\t SITUATION AND ORDER
\t 48th Tank Corps delivers a strong blow with its right flank on both sides of the Yakovlevo - Oboyan road northward, staves off opposing enemy tank forces at Psyol and occupies the line of hills between Kochetovka and to the north of Novoselovka. Then the corps keeps remains prepared to defeat 6th Guards Tank Corps standing on the western shore of the river in an enveloping attack. It is necessary to prevent the enemy from advancing across the river eastward. 
\t Grossdeutschland Division delivers the main blow at Novoselovka. After reaching the line of hills to the north of Novoselovka, it is ready to carry the advance forward with its left flank, passing Verkhopenye from northeast. To the right, 11th Tank Division advances to the east of the Yakovlevo - Oboyan roadway. 
\t The army commander emphasizes that command should not overexert the men and orders that the offensive not be planned for early in the morning, in order to give the forces a good night's rest.
\n 
\t COMBAT ORDER:
\t Withdrawn units of 67th Guards Rifle Division along with tank and antitank artillery groups have switched to the defensive in the sector to the south of Novoselovka, in the village area itself and on its northwest outskirts. The enemy defensive line's flanks are covered with minefields. 
Grossdeutschland continues the offensive along the western side of the roadway in the direction of Novoselovka. 
\n 
\t Captain Hartmann's combat team with the support of tanks and motorized infantry will advance to the west of roadway Yakovlevo - Oboyan in the direction of Novoselovka. By 14:00, occupy the line of hills 1km to the northwest of Novoselovka. 
\n 
\t Concept of operation: 
\t - reinforcements are Panther tanks, assault guns, rocket mortars; 
\t - use artillery fire and air strikes to destroy enemy positions to the south of Novoselovka; 
\t - having reached the southern outskirts of Novoselovka, ensure immediate cover for tanks and assault infantry teams; 
\t - press the advance towards the center of the village, destroy the antitank artillery, clear Novoselovka of enemy infantry; 
\t - with a concentrated attack occupy the enemy positions to the northwest of Novoselovka; 
\t - be ready to repel enemy tank counterattacks on the flanks. 
\n 
\t Supporting artillery and aircraft fire will be according to coordination signals. 
[Ger_Novoselovka.FullName]
Novoselovka 
[Ger_Kalinovka.Description]
\t July 10, 06:00. It is absolutely clear now, that the direct route to Kursk through Novoselovka and Oboyan is blocked by superior Russian forces. From now on 48th Tank Corps will perform missions in support of 2nd SS Tank Corps' offensive at Prokhorovka. There is hardly any chance that Hausser's corps will break through the Soviet defensive line in the Psyol river bend and overrun the large Russian tank reserves. 
\t The shift in the army's main efforts to the northeast means that we need to secure the rear area and the left flank from Soviet tank attacks. Grossdeutschland Division, which led the offensive before this, must distribute its forces on a wide front in order to surround 6th Tank Corps on the western shore of the Pena. The 4th Tank Army in its attempts to deal with threats from every direction unclenched its fist and spreads its fingers. 
\t Alas, the attack momentum of our forces is almost depleted in these violent fights. It is profitless efforts and inexcusable losses that depress the most. Only 132 of the 527 tanks we had before the beginning of the battle are left in tank regiments of 48th Tank Corps' divisions as of yesterday night. Tactical successes cannot cover the offensive's illusive strategic objectives. The two dozen kilometers we have advanced into the Russian steppe have no meaning.
\t The loss of hope has a negative impact on the morale of the soldiers and officers. Orders are still fulfilled in full obedience and with due care, but no one has any doubts that soon the blame game will begin, and the guilty names of those responsible for the operation's failure will be spoken. As the Führer cannot step up to the plate, army commanders will receive all the blame. It's no surprise that no one risks to lead the dance in this situation. But it is not enough to defeat the Russian army of today. 
\t Every day we see, that the Soviets have become well acquainted with our offensive patterns, and now they repel them in time with superior forces of tanks, artillery and infantry. There's hardly anything new in their tactics, though certain units demonstrate the virtue of training. But in operational planning they have proven to possess more forethought. We still haven't managed to find any weak points in the Russian defenses. Everywhere we run into organized defenses, minefields and constant attacks from the reserves. The prospects of this war in the East are very fearsome.
\n 
\t SUTIATION AND ORDER
\t Corps command decided to immediately deploy Grossdeutschland Division to the southwest in the direction of Kalinovka. The objective is Kalinovka and the hills to the south of it and to hold the withdrawing enemy.
\t The tank brigade advances through Novoselovka to the south of Kalinovka towards Hill 258.5. The reconnaissance battalion advances from Hill 251.4 in the direction of Kalinovka. The right flank of the fusilier regiment organizes all-round defenses in the vicinity of Novoselovka; its left flank does the same on Hill 251.4 with its front facing northwest. The grenadier regiment organizes all-round defenses on Hill 243.0 to the southeast of Kalinovka and covers the offensive in the northwest direction.
\t The artillery regiment supports the Panzerfuesilieres' and grenadiers' defenses and prevents the enemy from advancing from the fortified northern part of Verkhopenye.
\n 
\t COMBAT ORDER
\t In the sectors of Kruglik, Kalinovka, and Hill 232.8 isolated units of the 67th Guards Rifle Division with several groups of tanks from the 3rd Mechanized Corps stand on the defensive. The advancement of a new rifle division and the 10th Tank Corps to the line of Kruglik, Kalinovka has been spotted. 
\t Grossdeutschland Division advances in the southwest direction towards 3rd Tank Division with the task of surrounding the 6th Tank Corps. At the same time it protects the right wing from attacks of Russian tanks by occupying Hill 232.8. 
\t Captain Hartmann's combat team with tanks, motorized infantry and artillery will advance in the direction of Hill 232.8, Kalinovka. Defeat the enemy on the southeastern slopes of Hill 232.8 and advance to its northwestern slopes. Later, hold Hill 232.8, prevent enemy tanks and infantry from flanking the main division forces.
\n 
\t Concept of operation: 
\t - using artillery and air strikes, storm and defeat the enemy on Hill 232.8; 
\t - having reached the northeastern slopes of the hill, take the defensive and stand firmly on the occupied objective; 
\t - prevent enemy tanks and infantry from counterattacking from the northeast, prevent their advance towards the division's main forces; 
\t - prepare a mobile reserve to deny enemy maneuvers if he flanks the occupied positions; 
\t - the action is supported by rocket mortars and ground attack aircraft. 
\n 
\t Supporting artillery and air strikes will be according to coordination signals.
[Ger_Kalinovka.FullName]
Kalinovka
